// Which call site parks, and which wakes?
//
// Phase 16 established the shape from the syscall side: ~2.2 FUTEX_WAIT_BITSET (129) and
// ~2.2 FUTEX_WAKE_BITSET (137) per request on `tokio-rt-worker`, with `epoll_wait` at
// 0.04. Almost equal counts on both directions means symmetric park/wake *pairs* rather
// than a contended lock, but it does not say who is doing it. A parked thread and a
// waking thread are two different call sites, so they are counted apart.
//
// Op codes: 1 = FUTEX_WAKE, 129 = FUTEX_WAIT_BITSET (park), 137 = FUTEX_WAKE_BITSET (wake),
// 9 = FUTEX_WAIT_BITSET with a relative timeout in tokio's own spelling on some builds.
tracepoint:syscalls:sys_enter_futex
/comm == "tokio-rt-worker"/
{
    @op[args->op] = count();
    @by_op[args->op, ustack] = count();
}
